## Run

```bash
npm install          # or pnpm install
cp .env.example .env
npm run migrate      # create the schema (Knex migrations)
npm run dev          # start on http://localhost:4000
```

## Layout

```
src/
  server.ts            # entry point — YOURS to extend (written once, never overwritten)
  generated/           # owned by Backbone — regenerated wholesale, do not edit
    config/            # env + knex instance
    lib/               # HttpError + Fastify error handler
    schemas/           # zod create/update schemas + entity types
    models/            # repositories over Knex
    services/          # business layer
    controllers/       # Fastify route handlers
    routes/            # per-entity route plugins + aggregate index
<% if (auth) { -%>
    plugins/           # @fastify/jwt registration + `authenticate` preHandler
    auth/              # register / login / me
<% } -%>
migrations/            # additive, timestamped — never edited or deleted
scripts/migrate.ts     # runs knex migrate:latest
```

The API is assembled from Fastify plugins: each entity is a plugin registered by
`src/generated/routes/index.ts`, which `src/server.ts` mounts once.<% if (auth) { %> The auth plugin is registered
with `fastify-plugin` so its `authenticate` preHandler is available to the route plugins.<% } %>

Anything under `src/generated/` is overwritten every time you regenerate. Everything else is
yours. Add custom plugins and routes in `src/server.ts` where marked.

